{
  "analysis": "Inclusion is the bottleneck (recall 0.359, 130/179 missed) and its misses are overwhelmingly tiny faint vertical streaks (median missed 33.6px vs train 90.5px; low-size-tertile recall only 0.185 on n=146). Patches (0.72) and scratches (0.68) are stable but their low-size-tertile recall (~0.5) still lags, and both dipped slightly in R2 when starved, so they need a steady feed. R2's inclusion gain (+0.018) came from any_class backgrounds + prefer_small at a 0.45 min scale; the 0.35 min of R1 added unlearnable noise, so I keep min >=0.4 but bias small to hit the missed size regime.",
  "allocation": {"inclusion": 30, "patches": 10, "scratches": 10},
  "params": {
    "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.4, "scale_max": 0.9, "target_pool": "any_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": [11, 150, 268, 277, 297, 50, 99, 100, 106]},
    "patches": {"scale_min": 0.35, "scale_max": 0.95, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
    "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.35, "scale_max": 0.9, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []}
  },
  "rationale": "Spend the majority on inclusion (the only sub-0.4 class) but cap it near the ~80-cumulative diminishing-returns line (55+30=85) and keep patches/scratches at a non-starving 10 each so the shared detector doesn't regress. Inclusion: thin faint small sources (11,150,268,277,297,50,99,100,106) at 0.4-0.9 prefer_small on any_class backgrounds to match the small low-contrast missed streaks while avoiding R1's unlearnable 0.35 pastes. Patches/scratches: all sources with prefer_small to cover the small dark-blob and thin-line misses at learnable scales on same-class steel backgrounds."
}

The preview matches the missed defects well: inclusion pastes are thin, faint, small streaks (matching the 33.6px low-contrast misses), patches are dark blobs of varied size, and scratches are thin bright lines in vertical/horizontal/diagonal orientations. No pastes look unrealistic, oversized, or wasted. Sizes are in the learnable small-to-medium regime (no sub-0.35 noise). The plan is sound, so I repeat it unchanged.

